 1. threads before any Timeout.timeout call (names)      [nil]
 2. Timeout.timeout(0.2) { sleep 5 }                     Timeout::Error: execution expired
 3. after: the watcher thread exists (names)             [nil, "Timeout stdlib thread"]
 4. a block that finishes in time returns its value      :fast
 5. timeout(nil) / timeout(0) mean no limit              :a / :b
 6. your own class and message                           ArgumentError: too slow
 7. what the block sees / what the caller sees           ["inside rescued Timeout::ExitException", "inside ensure ran", "outside rescued Timeout::Error"]
 8. Timeout::Error's ancestors                           [Timeout::Error, RuntimeError, StandardError]
 9. a busy loop (no sleep) is interrupted too            Timeout::Error
10. Thread#kill: ensure runs; status / alive?            "ensure ran"; false / false
11. join(0.2) on a 5 s thread / alive?                   nil / true
12. Thread#wakeup ends a sleep with no limit             :woke
13. Thread#run ends a timed sleep early                  :sleep_cut_short
14. Thread#raise delivers an exception into a thread     "rescued RuntimeError: wake up"
15. Queue#pop(timeout: 0.2) on an empty queue            nil
